    (see scripts/generate_mecanum_rollers.py), not friction anisotropy. Roller count/
    radius/tilt are a simulation approximation, not a reverse-engineered match to the
    real ROSMASTER M3 Pro's physical roller wheels. The pin-placement radius is solved
    (not just WHEEL_RADIUS - ROLLER_RADIUS) so the effective rolling radius lands
    exactly on the nominal 0.04 m used in controllers.yaml's kinematics;
    see the cos(step/2) note in compute_geometry() before changing roller count/radius.
